{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BindingInteriorMaxObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BindingInteriorMaxObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ladder_miss_interior_max_nonmonotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ladder_miss_interior_max_nonmonotone","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingInteriorMaxObstruction.lean#L59-L69","doc":"**The interior maximum is genuine on the merged 3-ladder data.**\nThe neutron/deuteron/triton ladder misses each strictly exceed their `k=4` value at\n`k=3` (the witnessed facts `miss 4 < miss 3`, MeV values in the R10 witness and the\nR11-b audit), so each is non-monotone — a resonance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.miss_not_in_monotone_cone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.miss_not_in_monotone_cone","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingInteriorMaxObstruction.lean#L44-L57","doc":"**Interior-maximum obstruction (the certificate).**\nAny function `miss` with a strict decrease from `k=3` to `k=4` is **not** a\nnon-negative combination of functions non-decreasing in `k`: no such representation\nexists.  This is the scope-(b) exclusion of the monotone additive cone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.strict_decrease_not_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.strict_decrease_not_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingInteriorMaxObstruction.lean#L37-L42","doc":"**The Farkas functional `φ = e₄ − e₃`.**  For a monotone `g`, `g 3 ≤ g 4`;\nequivalently a strict decrease `g 4 < g 3` forces `g` to be non-monotone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.monotone_nonneg_combo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.monotone_nonneg_combo","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BindingInteriorMaxObstruction.lean#L25-L35","doc":"**A non-negative combination of monotone functions is monotone.**\nThe additive cone generated by functions non-decreasing in `k` consists of\nnon-decreasing functions. ","signatureChunk":0}]}